-- Row il-72. EXPECTED RED: two assertions that fail on purpose, one per item. Each says that no provision the citing words of section 27 name is repealed by an instrument deposited here, and each is FALSE.
-- I1: no section of the Criminal Procedure Ordinance (Evidence) that section 27(c) names is repealed.   False: one, section 4 (SH 444 section 12(2)).
-- I2: no provision of the Labour Department Ordinance that section 27(a) names is repealed.             False: one, section 10 (SH 164 section 41(1) names section 10 as a whole, which reaches 10 (1)).
-- The assertions test the list of provisions the citing words name against the instruments deposited. They do not evaluate section 25 of the Interpretation Law or say what a court would do.
-- The count, two, is declared in check.sh (expected_failed) and in encoding.json (expected_red). If a defect is cured by a later instrument, its assertion turns green and the declared count must go down with it.

